.SS _module.args
Additional arguments passed to each module in addition to ones like
\f[CR]lib\f[R], \f[CR]config\f[R], and \f[CR]pkgs\f[R],
\f[CR]modulesPath\f[R].
.PP
This option is also available to all submodules.
Submodules do not inherit args from their parent module, nor do they
provide args to their parent module or sibling submodules.
The sole exception to this is the argument \f[CR]name\f[R] which is
provided by parent modules to a submodule and contains the attribute
name the submodule is bound to, or a unique generated name if it is not
bound to an attribute.
.PP
Some arguments are already passed by default, of which the following
\f[I]cannot\f[R] be changed with this option:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]lib\f[R]: The nixpkgs library.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]config\f[R]: The results of all options after merging the values
from all modules together.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]options\f[R]: The options declared in all modules.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]specialArgs\f[R]: The \f[CR]specialArgs\f[R] argument passed to
\f[CR]evalModules\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
All attributes of \f[CR]specialArgs\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Whereas option values can generally depend on other option values thanks
to laziness, this does not apply to \f[CR]imports\f[R], which must be
computed statically before anything else.
.PP
For this reason, callers of the module system can provide
\f[CR]specialArgs\f[R] which are available during import resolution.
.PP
For NixOS, \f[CR]specialArgs\f[R] includes \f[CR]modulesPath\f[R], which
allows you to import extra modules from the nixpkgs package tree without
having to somehow make the module aware of the location of the
\f[CR]nixpkgs\f[R] or NixOS directories.
.IP
.EX
{ modulesPath, ... }: {
  imports = [
    (modulesPath + \(dq/profiles/minimal.nix\(dq)
  ];
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
For NixOS, the default value for this option includes at least this
argument:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]pkgs\f[R]: The nixpkgs package set according to the
\f[CR]nixpkgs.pkgs\f[R] option.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] lazy attribute set of raw value
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{ }
.EE
.PP
