/modules/common.nix
.UE \c
.SS clean\-src\-ignore\-files
The ignore files read when \f[CR]clean\-src\f[R] is enabled, relative to
the root of the source tree.
Every pattern is interpreted with the root as its base, whichever file
it came from, so an anchored pattern in a nested file
(\f[CR]dist/*\f[R]) matches against the root rather than against the
directory the file sits in; where that matters, give the pattern through
\f[CR]clean\-src\-patterns\f[R] instead.
.PP
