.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
[
  \(dq/.gitignore\(dq
]
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Example:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
[
  \(dq/.gitignore\(dq
  \(dq/frontend/.gitignore\(dq
]
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/common.nix
/modules/common.nix
.UE \c
.SS clean\-src\-patterns
Extra gitignore\-syntax patterns, applied on top of the files
\f[CR]clean\-src\-ignore\-files\f[R] names, when \f[CR]clean\-src\f[R]
is enabled.
A bare pattern (\f[CR]dist\-js\f[R]) matches at any depth, which is what
an anchored one read against the root cannot do.
.PP
