/modules/haskell.nix
.UE \c
.SS haskell\-nix.options.evalSrc
Allows a different version of the src to be used at eval time.
This is useful when building the source may require a build machine.
To avoid an eval time dependency on a build machine set
\f[CR]evalSrc\f[R] to either:
.IP \(bu 2
A version of the source built using \f[CR]evalPackages\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
A version of the source that does not require building
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] absolute path or package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
<nix\-haskell>
.EE
.PP
