.SS nixpkgs.compiler\-version
The version of the compiler this driver builds with.
Both drivers answer to the same name, and each answers for itself: they
mirror \f[CR]compiler\f[R] separately and fall back to different
compilers of their own, so a project asking what it is building against
asks the driver:
.IP
.EX
config.<driver>.compiler\-version
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] string
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R] the version \f[CR]compiler.version\f[R] states, or
the one carried by the compiler the driver resolves: the package a
project brought, or the \f[CR]ghc\f[R] of the package set it selected
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/nixpkgs
/modules/nixpkgs
.UE \c
.SS nixpkgs.cross\-compiler
The compiler this driver builds a cross target with, by
\f[CR]pkgs.pkgsCross\f[R] name.
Both drivers answer to the same name, so a step that needs the compiler
an artifact was built with, as \f[CR]wasm\-jsffi\f[R] does, asks for it
the same way whichever driver built the artifact:
.IP
.EX
config.<driver>.cross\-compiler \(dqwasi32\(dq
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] function that evaluates to a(n) package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
platform: config.nixpkgs.project.projectCross.<platform>.haskellPackages.ghc
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/nixpkgs
/modules/nixpkgs
.UE \c
.SS nixpkgs.cross\-exe
What this driver builds an executable into, for one cross target.
Both drivers answer to the same name, and what they answer with carries
the executable at \f[CR]bin/<exe>\f[R], with a wasm target\(cqs binary
at \f[CR]bin/<exe>.wasm\f[R] and a javascript target\(cqs linked
directory at \f[CR]bin/<exe>.jsexe\f[R].
It is what \f[CR]bundles\f[R] optimizes.
.PP
This driver builds one derivation per package, so the executable\(cqs
own name says nothing about where to look; it is taken for the sake of
the one interface both drivers answer to.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] function that evaluates to a(n) package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{ platform, package, exe }:
  config.nixpkgs.project.projectCross.<platform>.packages.<package>
.EE
.PP
