.SS platforms.<name>.packages.<name>.closure.extraFlags
Flags appended after the level and the externs, so one of these decides
what they would have.
One flag per element, its value in the same string, since the elements
are joined into one command line.
.PP
The default accepts whatever syntax the linker emitted, keeps the
compiler quiet, wraps the program in a function expression it may assume
nothing escapes from, asks for strict mode, and stops it complaining
about the names the runtime defines elsewhere.
