.SS platforms.<name>.wasm\-opt.extraFlags
Flags appended after \f[CR]\-all \-O<level>\f[R], so one of these
decides what the level would have.
One flag per element, its value in the same string, since the elements
are joined into one command line.
.PP
The default asks for the optimize level of \f[CR]\-O2\f[R] at the shrink
level of \f[CR]\-O1\f[R], drops the memory a module never reads,
discards debug information, and repeats the passes until they stop
finding anything.
.PP
\f[CR]null\f[R] states nothing, leaving the field to the layer beneath
it, and last to the tool\(cqs own settings at the top level.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] null or (list of string)
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
null
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/common.nix
/modules/common.nix
.UE \c
.SS platforms.<name>.wasm\-opt.level
The \f[CR]\-O\f[R] level wasm\-opt runs at.
.PP
