.SS shell.packages
Package selection function.
It takes a set of Haskell packages and returns a subset of these
packages with all of their dependencies included in
\f[CR]ghc\-pkg list\f[R].
It can take either a \f[CR]package\f[R] or name (\f[CR]string\f[R]) of a
package which availability can depend on the platform.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] null or unspecified value
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R] \f[CR]null\f[R] (all local packages that are not
\f[CR]source\-repository\-packages\f[R] are selected)
.PP
\f[I]Example:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
ps: with ps; [
  common
  frontend
  \(dqbackend\(dq # Provided by name so that it is only included when it\(aqs among \(gaps\(ga
]
.EE
.PP
