.SS source\-repository\-packages
Local packages to add to the project.
A source is anything \f[CR]inputs\f[R] accepts, so a packed thunk
directory can be given as\-is and is resolved to the source it pins.
.PP
\f[CR]subdir\f[R] selects packages within the source, so a
multi\-package repository needs one entry rather than one per package.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] attribute set of (absolute path or (attribute set))
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{ }
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Example:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{
  obelisk\-frontend = deps.obelisk + \(dq/lib/frontend\(dq;
  obelisk\-backend = {
    src = deps.obelisk + \(dq/lib/backend\(dq;
    condition = \(dq!arch(javascript)\(dq;
  };

  reflex\-dom = deps.reflex\-dom + \(dq/reflex\-dom\(dq;
  reflex\-dom\-core = deps.reflex\-dom + \(dq/reflex\-dom\-core\(dq;
  reflex = deps.reflex;
}
.EE
.PP
