\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/common.nix
/modules/common.nix
.UE \c
.SS wasm\-jsffi
The \f[CR]ghc_wasm_jsffi.js\f[R] a GHC\-built wasm module needs to be
instantiated at all, read out of the binary by the compiler that built
it:
.IP
.EX
wasm\-jsffi {
  ghc = config.<driver>.cross\-compiler \(dqwasi32\(dq;
  wasm = \(dq${frontend}/bin/frontend.wasm\(dq;
}
.EE
.PP
The compiler must be the one that produced the binary, which is what
\f[CR]<driver>.cross\-compiler\f[R] names.
Run this on the binary as linked, before \f[CR]wasm\-optimize\f[R]
strips the sections it reads.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] function that evaluates to a(n) package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
<nix\-haskell>/libs/wasm\-jsffi.nix
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/cross/wasm
/modules/cross/wasm
.UE \c
.SS wasm\-opt.enable
Whether \f[CR]wasm\-optimize\f[R] runs wasm\-opt and the strip that
follows it at all.
When false it copies its input through, so what a caller installs sits
in the same place either way.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] boolean
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
true
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/cross/wasm
/modules/cross/wasm
.UE \c
.SS wasm\-opt.extraFlags
Flags appended after \f[CR]\-all \-O<level>\f[R], so one of these
decides what the level would have.
One flag per element, its value in the same string, since the elements
are joined into one command line.
.PP
The default asks for the optimize level of \f[CR]\-O2\f[R] at the shrink
level of \f[CR]\-O1\f[R], drops the memory a module never reads,
discards debug information, and repeats the passes until they stop
finding anything.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] list of string
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
[
  \(dq\-ol 2\(dq
  \(dq\-s 1\(dq
  \(dq\-\-low\-memory\-unused\(dq
  \(dq\-\-strip\-dwarf\(dq
  \(dq\-\-converge\(dq
]
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/cross/wasm
/modules/cross/wasm
.UE \c
.SS wasm\-opt.level
The \f[CR]\-O\f[R] level wasm\-opt runs at.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] one of \(lq0\(rq, \(lq1\(rq, \(lq2\(rq, \(lq3\(rq,
\(lq4\(rq, \(lqs\(rq, \(lqz\(rq
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
\(dq2\(dq
.EE
